  "statement": "The strongest version of Skeptic's demand is this: a deployment freeze whose legitimacy only the cleared room can confirm is functionally identical to a freeze the public must take on faith — and faith is exactly what thirty years of buried Volkswagen emissions numbers and rubber-stamped pre-Sarbanes-Oxley audits should have taught us never to extend. If the only people who can verify the trigger fired are the same people who pulled it, the architecture is a black box wearing an oversight costume. That objection is correct, and meeting it requires a schema, not a reassurance. So here is the schema. The public tier publishes the audit PROTOCOL, not the audit RESULT. It attests: evaluation class fired against pre-registered baseline number 7, control group held internet access, severity tier 3 of 4, deployment frozen on date X. The verification object is the process — was the registered protocol followed, was the baseline the one filed before the eval ran, does the severity band match the protocol's own scoring rubric. An outsider confirms internal consistency the way a reader of a published CVSS vector string confirms a severity score without ever receiving the proof-of-concept exploit, and the way an FDA adverse-event filing confirms a trial endpoint was hit without printing the molecule's synthesis route.",
