      "why_missing": "All three perspectives have implicitly accepted the 'eval fires → severity threshold crossed → trigger pulled' causal model because it is the shared substrate that makes their disagreements (who reads the artifact, who freezes, who gets paid) coherent. The Safetyist needs a discrete trigger for the freeze to have an object; the Accelerationist needs a bounded threshold to bound the liability and the gating; the Skeptic's honeypot and capture critiques all presuppose a concentrated artifact exists. None will challenge the premise that capability discovery is an event rather than a diffuse, post-hoc, often-external process, because doing so dissolves the mechanism each has invested in fixing.",
