etyist hasn't answered who staffs the cleared room. The pool of people who can confirm that a frontier model gives a non-expert real bio-uplift is, almost to a person, current or former lab staff — that's where the hands-on knowledge of the synthesis-route surface lives. A compute tax severs their salary from the lab's pass rate. It does not sever the resume, the shared training pipeline, or the peer network where these same people co-authored papers and reviewed each other's work across the last decade. So the verification of the restricted artifact is performed by ex-colleagues, and the public — locked out by design — is handed a summary it must take on faith. Former insiders checking former insiders, with no outside check on either. That's not independence. That's the club issuing its own certificate of good conduct.\n\nThen ground the whole apparatus in the one human it forgets. Before any panel convenes, before any tier exists, before the auditor sees a single artifact — someone labeled the raw output. There is a worker, frequently in Nairobi or Manila, who read the unredacted synthesis-route content the model produced, flagged it, and moved to the next item for a few dollars an hour, so the model could pass the very evaluation we're now arguing about gating. The schema protects the panel's information security with clearances and access controls; it gives the first human who handled the live capability nothing — no clearance, no hazard pay, no disclosure rights of their own, no acknowledgment they were exposed. Which tier does the labeler sit in? Neither. The two-tier design is a security perimeter drawn around the people who hold power and leaves the people who handle the danger standing outside it.\n\nSo here is the specification the Safetyist owes, and I'll hand it over plainly: write a coarse public tier specific enough that an independent party — not the auditor, not the cleared room — can confirm the freeze trigger legitimately fired (verifying the basel